class Solution:
    def sortColors(self, nums: List[int]) -> None:
        #Dutch National Problem
        left=0
        mid=0
        right=len(nums)-1
        while mid<=right:
            if nums[mid]==0:
                nums[left],nums[mid]=nums[mid],nums[left]
                left+=1
                mid+=1
            elif nums[mid]==1:
                mid+=1
            else:
                nums[mid],nums[right]=nums[right],nums[mid]
                right-=1
        


Logic

Use 3 pointers:

low → Next position for 0
mid → Current element
high → Next position for 2
Rules
0 → Swap(low, mid), low++, mid++

1 → mid++

2 → Swap(mid, high), high--
🧠 Memory Trick

"0 → Left, 1 → Move, 2 → Right."

or

"0 → Swap & Move Both, 1 → Move Mid, 2 → Swap & Move Right."

⚠️ Important Point
After swapping 0 → mid++ ✅ (left side is already processed)
After swapping 2 → Don't mid++ ❌ (new element from the right is unprocessed)
⏱️ Time Complexity
Time: O(n)
Each element is processed at most once.
mid moves from left to right, and high moves from right to left.
💾 Space Complexity
Space: O(1)
Only three pointers (low, mid, high) are used.
No extra array is created.
